These seven documents give you a complete blueprint for building **Echo Engine v1.0** — from the core audio library through the mobile-first Sound Lab application. The architecture keeps everything modular and dependency-free while the implementation guide includes the key code patterns (audio graph construction, noise/reverb generation, modulation routing, event automation) so you can start building immediately.

The key design decisions baked in:
- **Zero external dependencies** — pure Web Audio API
- **Mobile-first** — touch sliders, bottom nav, safe area insets, audio unlock, PWA
- **Audio-thread scheduling** — all time-based changes use Web Audio ramps (survive frame drops)
- **Seeded variation** — Mulberry32 PRNG for reproducible sessions
- **Parametric presets** — JSON format with URL sharing